%I A401001 #10 Oct 18 2026 23:15:54
%S A401001 1,2,3,4,8,16,64,114,190,204,294,366,378,390,554,1470,1650
%N A401001 Numbers k such that the sum of digits of k in base b is not prime for any base b in the range 2 <= b <= floor(sqrt(k)).
%C A401001 A number k is pernicious in base b if the sum of its digits in base b is prime. This sequence gives numbers that are non-pernicious across all bases 2 <= b <= floor(sqrt(k)), which corresponds to bases where n has at least three digits.
%C A401001 The upper bound floor(sqrt(n)) avoids trivial two-digit bases: for any k >= 5, the base b = k - 2 yields the two-digit representation 12_b with digit sum 1 + 2 = 3, which is always prime. Similarly, base b = k - 4 gives digit sum 5, and base b = n - 6 gives digit sum 7. Without restricting the base to b <= floor(sqrt(k)), no integer k >= 5 could qualify.
%C A401001 For k <= 3, the condition holds vacuously because the range 2 <= b <= floor(sqrt(k)) is empty.
%C A401001 Conjectured to be finite, with 1650 being the last term; no further terms exist up to k = 50000.
%e A401001 4 is in the sequence: floor(sqrt(4)) = 2; in base 2, 4 is 100_2 with digit sum 1 + 0 + 0 = 1 (not prime).
%e A401001 5 is not in the sequence: floor(sqrt(5)) = 2; in base 2, 5 is 101_2 with digit sum 1 + 0 + 1 = 2 (prime).
%e A401001 114 is in the sequence: floor(sqrt(114)) = 10; the digit sums in bases 2 through 10 are 4, 4, 6, 10, 4, 6, 9, 10, 6, none of which is prime.
%t A401001 Select[Range[2000], Function[n, NoneTrue[Range[2, Floor[Sqrt[n]]], PrimeQ[Total[IntegerDigits[n, #]]] &]]]
%o A401001 (Python)
%o A401001 from math import isqrt
%o A401001 from sympy import isprime
%o A401001 def digit_sum(n, b):
%o A401001     s = 0
%o A401001     while n > 0:
%o A401001         s += n % b
%o A401001         n //= b
%o A401001     return s
%o A401001 def ok(n):
%o A401001     for b in range(2, isqrt(n) + 1):
%o A401001         if isprime(digit_sum(n, b)):
%o A401001             return False
%o A401001     return True
%o A401001 print([k for k in range(1, 2001) if ok(k)])
%Y A401001 Cf. A000040, A000120, A007953, A052294.
%K A401001 nonn,base,new
%O A401001 1,2
